Z||000000||JSocha||05-10-2001||10:46 AM||||I'm just wondering as she lately has been leaving little red spots all over my garage and driveway and I am not as familiar with this breed as alot of you out here are, as I only adopted her this past November after a lifelong love for this breed.<P>I'm sure with her now being 14 years old she is at that mature age now where things like this are bound to happen and she has been a little moody lately...and since I don't know if she has done this before...I am thinking...<P>Perhaps I should find her a male counterpart and see if I can breed the two to see what kind of offspring they will produce (as somebody on this forum said they are related to rabbits and multiply as such...do they?).<P>Anybody out there got a stud with good fluid lines to mate these two with to see what they would produce?  Don't want any Ugo's or Miata's off springs popping up, so the stud has to come from good clean stock.<P>Not to sound, be prejudice or the like (as I relize we all have different ethnic backgrounds with our cars here), but I would like to breed her with the same or simlar color at this time as she has a "Medium Red Metallic" complexion to see what she may throw, besides possibly a bearing.<P>How much would someone out there charge me to put their Fiero out for stud?<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||5
