Z||000009||JSocha||05-11-2001||09:39 AM||||Yes!<P>I agree with you, your Fiero would be a fine looking stud  and possibility for my little 87 beauty.  Nice lines, good conformity and sounds like a good "winning" background and "Pedigree" in his tranny lines.  How old is he?  Any recent and severe medical problems?  How much has he been ridden?<P>Most importantly, what's your Fiero's aggressiveness level?  By the picture, he looks agressive and that is a concern for me as I have one daughter (Freshman this fall) left who is learning to drive this summer.  I'm worried the offspring from this mating could be more then what she could possibly/eventually handle on the streets if the offspring is born with two much power in the hind quarters.<P>How about responsiveness out of the approach, turning and responding to the driver?<P>As far as litter size, I believe only one, unless twins occur (but I am working on getting that clarified to ensure they aren't related to the VW Rabbit), otherwise to insure many of them at once could get to be expensive.<P>I will keep you on my list of potentials and I would like to get some other possibilities to choose from first before making a final decision to make sure the right balance and blue print are in place.  The was she is spotting now, I think she will be in heat for awhile.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> ||||reg||1
